From 792d65121fa6cc3fdf5ec8680c400c731753d18e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego <me@diegonmarcos.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 10:55:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] comms: RSS folders reach mail-folder parity + Accounts tab +
 edit + update robustness
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. Folder parity — RSS leaf folders now created with notify=true + navigation=true
   (show as nav-menu shortcuts + raise new-item notifications, same as mail
   folders; both togglable per-folder). Feeds account notify=true.
   repairRssAccount upgrades pre-0056 installs (setFolderNotify/Navigation +
   setAccountNotify) so existing users get parity without re-subscribing.
2. RSS account 'edit properties' (long-press → edit) was a silent no-op
   (onEditAccount case TYPE_RSS: return). Now opens the Cloud Feeds manager.
3. Configuration: new 'Accounts' tab inserted at index 1 (after Main, before
   Receive) hosting FragmentAccounts — a shortcut to the accounts screen.
4. Auto-update robustness: the 6h background updater's install-confirm dialog
   was launched via startActivity from a receiver — blocked by Android 10+
   background-activity-launch, so an update needing the 'install unknown apps'
   confirmation died invisibly. CommsInstallReceiver now falls back to a
   tap-to-install notification (PendingIntent), which works from the background.

Tester: test-rss-folder-parity.sh 17/17.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
